# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-15), from the product owner's decisions in collab/QUESTIONS.md (Q16, Q20, Q21; the note of 2026-10-15 on F48); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: a frame a person gives a window while Arbor is not running, or paused, is its own from then on. An editor is docked; the notes
# were never docked. In the evening the person quits Arbor and pushes the notes somewhere else. In the morning Arbor starts: the notes are not moved,
# and from now on that is their place: framing the editor and showing everything brings them back there, not to where they lay yesterday.
# Reference: T60, issue #3 rule 2.
open Editor 700x500
open Notes 500x300
dock 101 left
move 102 800 100 500 300
relaunch quit
expect ok
move 102 860 520 500 300
relaunch start
expect ok
expect still 102
expect docked 101
expect floating 102
expect at 102 860 520
zoom 101
expect hidden 102
show-all
expect at 102 860 520
expect size 102 500x300
# Made smaller while Arbor is away: the size is theirs too.
relaunch quit
move 102 900 400 420 260
relaunch start
expect still 102
expect at 102 900 400
zoom 101
show-all
expect at 102 900 400
expect size 102 420x260
# The same during a pause, which is as if Arbor had quit, and it comes back.
pause
move 102 820 200 420 260
resume
expect still 102
expect at 102 820 200
zoom 101
show-all
expect at 102 820 200
# At the desk, with a second display to the right: the notes float there.
displays 2
move 102 1700 300 420 260
# The display is unplugged: the notes come to the one that is left. Arbor is quit.
displays 1
wait 3
expect visible 102
relaunch quit
# Back at the desk the display is plugged in while Arbor is not running, and the person keeps the notes on the first display.
displays 2
move 102 880 480 420 260
relaunch start
# That the display which is back remembers a place for the notes moves nothing.
expect still 102
expect at 102 880 480
expect size 102 420x260
expect docked 101
zoom 101
show-all
expect at 102 880 480
# A start without a quit before it is a slip in the script, and says so.
relaunch start
expect fail
